UID:10188-1789671600-1789677000@thespaceforart.com
SUMMARY:Tea & Tarot - A Bookclub Style Discussion Group
DESCRIPTION:Monthly Gathering | Thursday\, September 17th | 7:00 PM – 8:30 PM | The Space | $25 \nCalling all tarot lovers\, both new and seasoned!  Join us for an intimate way of exploring the cards. \nWhat could be better than a cozy evening of warm tea and deep conversation? Join us for Tea & Tarot with Gina Devine—a monthly\, book club-style discussion group created to deepen our connection with the archetypes of the tarot through community and shared insight. \nRather than a formal class\, this is a casual meet-up where we treat the tarot as a living text. Based on the psychological insights of Carl Jung\, we will explore the Major Arcana not just as fortune-telling tools\, but as mirrors of our own lives\, rituals\, and transformations. \nThe Experience \nEach month\, we open a new gateway of creative and spiritual exploration. Our time together includes: \n\nArchetypal Deep Dives: We’ll focus on a specific theme or set of cards each session\, discussing their symbolism and how they show up in our modern world.\nCollaborative Readings: A chance to pull cards for one another in a supportive\, low-pressure environment.\nRitual & Connection: We’ll sip tea\, share stories\, and find common ground in the mysteries of the deck.\nIntuitive Growth: Whether you’ve been reading for decades or just bought your first deck\, you’ll leave with a deeper understanding of the “BodyGraph” of the tarot.\n\nWhat to Bring \nTo make the most of our evening\, please bring the following if you can: \n\nYour Tarot Deck: Any deck you feel connected to.  If you don’t have any we have some available here to use.\nYour Favorite Mug: We’ll provide a selection of teas\, and don’t worry if you don’t bring your mug – we have those too!\nA Notebook: For capturing insights\, spreads\, and “aha” moments.\n\nInvestment: $25 \nStay Connected: Sign up for the Soul Centric Tarot Newsletter here. \nSpaces are limited to keep our discussion intimate and impactful. Reserve your spot today and join the circle. \nCover art by Sophie Bryant Funnell \n______________________________ \n\nYour Guide Gina Devine\nInstagram: @gina.devine \n\nGina Devine is an esoteric artist\, intuitive tarot reader\, writer\, educator and guide. \nShe has provided thousands of readings for people all over the world\, and leads both protection and tarot workshops. Her approach to guidance is loving\, grounded and human. Although she also teaches traditional tarot classes\, her tea and tarot discussion group was birthed from the knowing that people are more inclined to to be in tune with the archetypes of the cards and the messages they bring when they are allowed space to enjoy the tarot in a more casual setting – instead of forcefully trying to memorize them. The same way we find joy in discussing a book in community\, the cards also call for us to convene together around them. Her approach is philosophical\, therapeutic and creative\, and she is on a mission to guide people toward unearthing a more intimate and honest relationship with their inner knowing through the art of divination. You can find her services and more at soulcentrictarot.com
URL:https://thespaceforart.com/event/tea-tarot-a-bookclub-style-discussion-group/
LOCATION:the Space\, 356 Bloomfield Ave\, Montclair\, New Jersey\, 07042
CATEGORIES:Art,Wellness
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://thespaceforart.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Screenshot-2026-04-03-at-10.34.42-PM.png
END:VEVENT
