UID:10283-1792859400-1792866600@thespaceforart.com
SUMMARY:Writing the Body - A Writing Workshop for Women
DESCRIPTION:Writing the Body – A Writing Workshop for Women\nWhat can poetry say about our bodies that ordinary language can’t? How can our bodily experiences open new paths for our writing? \nIn this generative workshop for women and nonbinary writers\, Barbara O’Dair – poet\, writer\, and cofounder of the Park St. Writers Series – leads the group through readings\, discussion\, and writing exercises\, using prompts to reveal fresh language\, unexpected stories\, and adventurous forms\, and drawing from subjects such as body image\, sexuality\, desire\, gender\, illness\, health\, and aging. \nAfter a short grounding exercise\, we’ll read and discuss a few poems that use the body and bodily experience to create meaning and music. Then we’ll write short pieces from three or four prompts. Everyone is encouraged to read their work aloud\, and if time allows\, the poet can take a few questions about their piece from the group. \nAfter a five-minute break\, the second half of the workshop is devoted to writing a poem or creative piece and reading it aloud — either within the group\, or as a “test drive” for the open mic later that evening. \nA few of the prompts (we may not get to all of them): \n\nIf Your Body Could Talk… What would it say? Write a monologue in which one part of your body finally gets a chance to speak.\nThe Inherited Body. Finish this sentence: “I inherited my [body/hair/teeth] from…” Your parent is a natural choice\, but consider more surprising options too — neighborhood\, gender\, class.\nMedical Chart. Write a list of notes about your body that might appear on a medical chart\, from a doctor’s POV. Then write your version: what should we know about you and your body? What does your version tell us about you?\nYour Body in Time. Meet your body at eight\, 25\, 48\, and today (or\, if you’re under 40\, work out the right ages). Introduce your different bodies to each other. Maybe your 48-year-old body wants a word with your eight-year-old body. About what?\n\nWriting the Body – A Writing Workshop for Women \nSaturday\, October 24\, 4:30 – 6:30\, $44 – price includes admission to the open mic.   \nWorkshop participants will be invited to read their work at the Space for Words open mic for writers that will follow the workshop later the same evening at 8pm.  The first portion of the open mic will be for workshop participants\, and the second half is open to all women and female identifying persons. \nLearn more about the open mic here. \n \nBarbara O’Dair is a poet\, writer\, and cofounder of the Park St. Writers Series based in Montclair\, NJ.
URL:https://thespaceforart.com/event/writing-the-body-a-writing-workshop-for-women/
LOCATION:the Space\, 356 Bloomfield Ave\, Montclair\, New Jersey\, 07042
CATEGORIES:Art,The Space for Words
