SUMMARY:The Space for Words Open Mic — Women's Edition
DESCRIPTION:The Space for Words Open Mic — Women’s Edition\nDoors 7:30 · Start 8 PM · $10 for everyone \nOur monthly open mic returns for a special edition dedicated to women and female-identifying writers. \nThe first portion of the night belongs to the workshop that is held before the open mic. Barbara O’Dair will lead a writing workshop that presents the theme ‘if your body could talk’.  Learn more about the workshop here.  Participants come up to read what they wrote that afternoon – new work\, still warm\, out loud for the first time. If you spent the evening writing about your body\, this is where it gets to be heard. \nThe second portion is open to all women and female-identifying persons. Bring your poetry\, short stories\, or excerpts from your latest work – the stage is yours. The Space is a safe place to try out new material\, read old favorites\, experiment with a different genre\, and even to sing a song if inspiration strikes you. Put your name in the basket on your way in and you’ll get a shot at the mic\, with a maximum of 5 minutes. Depending on how many people sign up and if time allows\, we can have people come up a second time. \nCome for the words\, stay for the community. The Space for Words has grown into an amazing community of writers supporting one another\, and this night is about turning that room over to women’s voices for an evening. All levels\, all genres — fiction\, non-fiction\, memoir\, poetry. Afterward we take time to socialize and vibe with one another. \nYou don’t have to do both. Come for the workshop\, come for the open mic\, or make a night of it. \n\nGood to know\nAudience members are\, as always\, a welcome and vital part of these performances. \nIf you have published books you’d like to sell\, bring some copies and be prepared to accept payment. \nGeneral guidelines: \n\nHate speech of any kind is never allowed and will be shut down.\nViolence or references to physical harm to others will be shut down.\n\nBYOB is welcome\, and some light snacks and drinks are served. \nAccessibility: The Space is located on the second floor of a historic building\, accessible via a flight of stairs. Unfortunately\, there is no elevator access at this time. This means we are unable to accommodate wheelchairs or guests with significant mobility challenges. We sincerely apologize for any inconvenience this may cause.
URL:https://thespaceforart.com/event/the-space-for-words-open-mic-night-for-wordsmiths/
LOCATION:the Space\, 356 Bloomfield Ave\, Montclair\, New Jersey\, 07042
CATEGORIES:The Space for Words
